# Turing Machine
One Machine acting like all machines. Reprogrammable, general purpose machine.

The program is stored in the ROM in the computer. The program here is the set of binary stored adress by adress. in the ROM which the CPU access adress by adress.

Q. How are we going to specify the instructions?
Q. How to perform the specified instruction at a given time?
Q. How to operate hardware using software?

Instruction in machine language are squences of bits

0100010 0011 0010 : Machine Language
ADD     R3   R2   : Assembly Language

Elements Of Machine Language:

Arithmetic Operations
Logical Operations
Flow COntrol


Memory Hiracrchy
Accessing memory is computationaly expensive.
accesing the memory consumes more time than the operations performed on them.
Solution: Memory Hirarchy

Register < Cache < Main Memory < Disk

CPU has few easily accessed registers.

What are the registers:

1. Data Registers: put numeber in it
2. Adress Registers: put adress of the main memory

how do we decide what data to work upn
Adressing mode

1. Register
    ADD REGISTER 1 to REGISTER 2 and Store in REGISTER 2

2. Direct 
    ADD REGISTER 1 to MEM[100] and store in MEM[100]

3. Indirect
    A is a another adreess
    ADD MEM[A] to REGISTER 2 and Sstore in MEM[A]

4. Immidiate
    ADD REG 1 to 3 and store in REG 1

Flow control
JUMP to instructions


Hack Machine Language:

Hack COmuter:

16 bit machine:
    1.Data Memory(RAM): Sequence of 16 bit registers
    2. Instruciton memory(ROM): 16 bit registers
    3. CPU: performs instructions
    4. bus: move data from one place to another
        1. Data bus CPU to memory
        2.instruction bus ROM TO CPUT
        3. Adress bus
    5.Reset

Registers:
1.D
    data value
2.A
    data or adress
3.M
    selected register


A instruciton:
'@'

Eg:
@21
effect:
SElects A register to 21
RAM 21 becomes the selecred ram 21

Usage expamle:
@100
M = -1

C instruction:

dest = comp ; jump

comp = All the alu operations
dest = null, M, D, MD, A, AM ,AD, AMD
jump = null, JGT, JEQ, JGE, JLT, JNT, JLR, JMP

example
@1 //set A register to 1
M=A-1;JEQ // computes A-1 and stores in M(which is RAM[A(1)])
          // Computation is 0 therefore JEQ causes jump to A which is one. 

Hack Language Specification:
A instruction
@value
non negative decimal contsant <= 32767

0 000000000000000
first 0 is opcode, it defines that this is A instruciton, rest all are the data value which stores the numenbr or adress numebr

1 1 1 a c1 c2 c3 c4 c5 c6 d1 d2 d3 j1 j2 j3
opcode, 2 bits not used, c= comp bits, d =destination, j=jump

There are some binary values which map the 6 c bits to the operation bits. this maps symbols to binary bits.
same is for the destination bits and the jump bits. 

Hack Program:

//initialization

//i is initialized to be 1 
@16     //select 16
M=1     // RAM[16] = 1

//sum is intitialized to be 0
@17     // Select 17
M=0     // RAM[17] = 0

//loop condition
@16     //Select 16
D=M     // D reg = RAM[16] (1?)
@0      //select 0 which is the n value. 
D=D-M   // i - n 
@17     //select 17
D;JGT   //if (i-n) > 0 then jump to 17

//addition operation
@16     //select 16
D=M     // D is RAM[16]
@17     //select 17
M=D+M   //RAM[17]  is RAM[16] plus RAM[17]
@16     // select  16
M=M+1   // RAM[16] is RAM[16] plus 1
@4      //Select 4
0;JMP   //JUMP to 4 unconditional

//end and RAM[1] value output
@17     //select 17
D=M     //D is RAM[17]
@1      // select 1
M=D     // RAM[1] = RAM[17]
@21     // select 21
0;JMP   //Jump to 21 unconditional



Controlling Input/Outpu devices using hack computer language.

1.Screen

Screen Memory Map

the display is refreshed with the screen memory map. 
Screen has 256x512

to set pixel (row,column) on/off
word = Screen[32*row + col/16]
word = RAM[16384 + word]
(col%16)th bit will be the target which we can turn on or off.

This memory map is stored in RAM


2. Keyboard Memory Map
When a key is pressed then the key's scan code is sent through the wire to the RAM register. when the keyboard is not being tpouched then the register is 0
the register is RAM[24576]


